            "name": "Boot or Logon Autostart Execution: Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder",
            "description": "[confidence=high, sources=dynamic,static] [from D3D11InstallHelper.dll] The malware string 'RegOpenKeyExW' was found in the binary, alongside 2 other string(s) also characteristic of Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder. Multiple corroborating strings, not this one in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal. | [from D3D11InstallHelper.dll] The malware string 'RegSetValueExW' was found in the binary, alongside 2 other string(s) also characteristic of Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder. Multiple corroborating strings, not this one in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal. | [from D3D11InstallHelper.dll] The malware string 'RegCreateKeyExW' was found in the binary, alongside 2 other string(s) also characteristic of Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder. Multiple corroborating strings, not this one in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal. | [from D3D11InstallHelper.dll] The API functions RegSetValueExW, RegOpenKeyExW, RegCreateKeyExW are all imported by the binary. This combination is characteristic of Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder \u2014 multiple corroborating APIs together, not one import in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal. | CAPE signature 'persistence_autorun' fired (severity=3, confidence=100%, categories=['persistence'])",
